    "reading": "Going from 5-grams to 9-grams pushes different-pairs down four times as far as same-pairs, so 9-grams genuinely separate better. But the bootstrap intervals on recall-at-zero-false-merges overlap, and 9-grams also drag the true-duplicate median down (0.903 -> 0.871). Every point of true-duplicate similarity lost has to be bought back with more LSH bands, and part (e) shows candidate volume -- not scoring -- is what threatens the 20-minute budget."
